diff --git a/docs/api_to_audit.md b/docs/api_to_audit.md
index f65816be5d091eeb793656b378aee691b4dfb89e..d05104a992c43db9106cb21c7ac1e7e6b6f19163 100644
--- a/docs/api_to_audit.md
+++ b/docs/api_to_audit.md
@@ -504,6 +504,47 @@ built-in checkout, worktree, and personal workspace behaviors are first-party
 plugins; legacy workspace request shapes are compatibility sugar resolved to
 those providers at the server boundary.
 
+## `bb.experimental_environmentGitObjects.inspect`
+
+**What it does.** Inspects named Git objects in one existing project source on
+the host that owns a ready environment. The request is fully pinned: callers
+name a project, registered source, ready environment, commit object ID and a
+bounded list of tree, blob, or diff selections. Core resolves the source root
+from its own records, verifies project and host identity, and sends that
+stored root to the enrolled host. The caller never supplies a repository path,
+ref, command, shell, working tree, remote, or network policy.
+
+The host resolves only a full commit ID and its tree, rejects unexpected tree
+or object IDs, and uses fixed Git plumbing with hooks, external diff/textconv,
+interactive prompts, optional locks, global/system configuration and file
+protocols disabled. It returns typed data with plugin/project/source/
+environment/host/source-root/commit/tree provenance, including the current canonical
+`origin` identity from the selected source's local Git configuration. The
+attestation accepts one non-credentialed HTTPS or Git-SSH remote, normalizes
+its host and repository path, and rejects missing, malformed, or multiple
+origin URLs. It does not consult cached project remote metadata, fetch, or
+resolve refs. Results are capped, non-streaming and all-or-nothing: a
+recursive tree that reaches the entry bound or a submodule, or any selection
+exceeding the output limit, returns an explicit unavailable result rather than
+a partial proof. LFS pointers are labels for the committed pointer only; no LFS
+content is fetched. An old or mismatched host protocol, missing
+environment/source, identity mismatch, unavailable host or missing object also
+fails closed. This surface never creates a terminal or uses a generic plugin
+RPC fallback.
+
+**Audit before stabilizing.**
+
+1. Review each caller's authorization to inspect the selected project source;
+   this API proves host/source identity, not repository-review policy.
+2. Verify SHA-1 and SHA-256 repositories, empty and nested trees, binary blobs,
+   diffs, object-type confusion, malformed paths, symbolic IDs, output limits,
+   timeouts, submodules and LFS pointers.
+3. Confirm no operation mutates refs, index, worktree, Git configuration or
+   network state, including hostile repository configuration and hooks.
+4. Exercise mixed old/new SDKs and server/host protocol versions, plus
+   disconnected hosts, to retain explicit unavailable outcomes rather than a
+   terminal, shell or advisory read-only fallback.
+
 **Audit before stabilizing.**
 
 1. **Requirement vocabulary.** `requires` has four booleans, each a fact core
